<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n436" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγέλ-η</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>herd</i>, of horses, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				19.281
			</span></i>; elsewhere in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always of oxen and kine, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.678
			</span></i>, etc., cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βούνομος:</span>—also, <i>any herd</i> or
				<i>company</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συῶν ἀ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				168
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. παρθένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					112
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαινάδων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					1022
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτηνῶν ἀγέλαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					168
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				106
			</span></i>; <i>shoal</i> of fish, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				3.639
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνων ἀγέλαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					1276
				</span></i>
			:—also in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				451c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				570a27
			</span></i>, etc., but rare in early Prose. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in Crete and at Sparta, <i>bands</i> in
			which boys were trained, <i><span class="en">
				Ephor.
				64
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heraclid.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				4952
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Dreros</span>), etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέων ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					223.8
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Miletus</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀϊθέων</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				239
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Smyrna</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστρικαὶ σφαῖραι</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				43.6
			</span></i>.</div>
